    }
   },
   "source": [
    "What is LayoutLMv3, Donut, GPT-V, Qwen-VL?\n",
    "1. LayoutLMv3: A model that understands text + layout (position) + image of documents.\n",
    "2. Donut (Document Understanding Transformer): A model that reads documents without OCR and directly gives structured output.\n",
    "3. GPT-V (Vision GPT / GPT-4V type): A model that understands both images and text together\n",
    "4. Qwen-VL: Similar to GPT-V, but developed by Alibaba — works on image + text tasks"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "ae17ce53-8b0f-4dda-bf3d-68b2a8b98573",
   "metadata": {
    "vscode": {
     "languageId": "raw"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "If I need to move GBs or TBs of data from an on-premise SQL database to a cloud server, What will I do?\n",
    "\n",
    "For a large SQL on-premise dataset, I would first perform a full load using chunking and bulk transfer. \n",
    "I would export data in Parquet format, upload it to cloud storage such as S3, and then use bulk loading \n",
    "into the target database. After the initial migration, I would implement incremental loads using timestamps \n",
    "or CDC (Change Data Capture) to transfer only new or updated records. This approach is scalable, \n",
    "memory-efficient, and suitable for production environments."
   ]
  },
